nal dependency.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u31"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The circular defines distributors by distribution of SFC-authorised funds, while its account of paragraph 3.11 uses investment-product language. The competing readings differ on whether this selected control extends to those distributors’ promotions of other investment products.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u14","u15","u29"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Additional returns and incentives may constitute gifts; the text does not make that classification automatic. Product-type linkage expressly includes certain fund types and funds from certain fund houses. Gift, discount, and the full limits of linkage remain undefined.","source_unit_ids":["u8","u13","u14"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The fee-or-charge discount exception attaches to gifts in the selected control. Section 103 authorisation or exemption is a separate exception and does not excuse a gift-control failure. Whether rebates or mixed benefits qualify as discounts remains unresolved.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u14","u15"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The selected provision says distributors should not offer gifts; it is modeled as a selected conduct-control screen, without equating it to the separate statutory offence. The phrase may be considered preserves judgment about gift classification; actual investor distraction is not stated as a necessary condition.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u13","u14","u15","u24"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"30 September 2010 dates the referenced FAQ’s issuance, not commencement of this circular or the selected control. No circular issue date, effective date, transition period, or applicable Code version is supplied.","source_unit_ids":["u30","u31"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The complete paragraph 3.11 and FAQ questi